Gameplay 4.1.0 / UI 16.0
4.1 focuses on balance and choice quality rather than adding more content. Four ancestries, five independent origins, forty manually selected realm talents, sixteen sub-schools, six hybrid recipes and eight resource-conversion artifacts remain intact.
A permanent 500-run deterministic matrix now covers 4 ancestries x 5 origins x 25 seeds. Baseline race spread 24.8pp is reduced to 10.4pp; origin win-rate range 23%-94% is reduced to 55%-73% under the same fixed autoplay policy.
Final matrix: overall 60.4%; human 62.4%, spirit 56.8%, dragon 66.4%, ling 56.0%. Warrior now starts with fist + guard only, leaving the auxiliary slot to be built during the run; weaker starts receive identity-consistent early-loop support.
Verified: 140/140 rule tests, 500-run balance regression gate with no failures, and 53/53 HTTP Chromium UI checks.
4.1 uses a new deterministic save namespace. 4.0 and older saves are not imported into the new rules but remain exportable as backups.
